ref 17592186542866 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543325 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "35f6b671-0fc0-5734-b06f-e7fe4838a002" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543377 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186542706 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543377 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186542752 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543377 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186542949 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543377 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186543017 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543377 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186543085 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543377 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543377 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543377 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186542706 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543377 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "7e998d72-50f3-55e6-8d59-b1ab24f7504c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543440 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186542680 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543440 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186542850 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543440 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186542952 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543440 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186543153 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543440 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186543264 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543440 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543440 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543440 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186543264 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543440 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c8e8e57f-c7b6-551b-bce9-5ffb5155b1cc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543452 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186542698 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543452 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186542782 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543452 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186542917 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543452 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186543123 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543452 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186543185 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543452 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543452 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543452 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186542917 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543452 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e47b3773-65aa-5f66-b8a4-eb883505683f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543501 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186543377 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543501 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75176" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543501 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543501 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[1,4]\\times [2,4]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=x+2y-3.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{1,2,3,4\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{2,3,4\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the upper Riemann sum $U(f,P).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543501 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4bd06db2-69af-51a2-9fd5-21474b678038" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543501 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](images/89/89c82b8d1f3eaf79c7df0a67f377a240a949dda328cd2f448370077d2871c244.png)\n\nThe upper sum $U(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={M}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{M}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{M}_{31}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{31}) \\\\  & \\,+{M}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{M}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22})+{M}_{32}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{32}),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *maximum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *upper* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=1$ for all $6$ subregions, the formula for $U(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={M}_{11}+{M}_{21}+{M}_{31}+{M}_{12}+{M}_{22}+{M}_{32}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=x+2y-3$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=x+2y-3$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/78/7888eaa17b26267cc8bed166500ba504fe5a893b30eb90876f2074520e28e8ba.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/ea/eadef808ebc8ff5503de8cefbbbf3a1d64bf3149f0c0c80166c891550ddee91d.png)\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{11} & =f(2,3)=5 \\\\ {M}_{21} & =f(3,3)=6 \\\\ {M}_{31} & =f(4,3)=7 \\\\ {M}_{12} & =f(2,4)=7 \\\\ {M}_{22} & =f(3,4)=8 \\\\ {M}_{32} & =f(4,4)=9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & =5+6+7+7+8+9 \\\\  & =42.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543539 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186543325 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543539 #edb/ref 1069 "q-123053" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543539 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543539 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/fe/fe238b0f1c4a9c34f569c9f4c4655f4a6094ee00a225a0d418fff7276705060d.png)\n\nConsider the partition of the rectangular region $R$ shown above and the positive function $f(x,y)$ defined on $R.$ Which of the following gives an expression for the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to this partition.\n\n*Hint: ${M}_{ij}$ denotes the maximum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}$*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543539 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a3ec1567-3655-5115-83b3-81bdfee12880" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543539 #edb/ref 1074 "To calculate the upper Riemann sum $U$ with respect to the given partition, we compute the sum of the volumes of $4$ rectangular solids, one for each ${R}_{ij}.$\n\nThe volume of the rectangular solid corresponding to each subregion ${R}_{ij}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{ij}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{ij}).\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ denotes the maximum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *maximum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *upper* sum.\n\nSo in our case, we have\n\n$$\nU={M}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{M}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{M}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{M}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22}).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{11})=\\text{Area}({R}_{21})=2\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{12})=\\text{Area}({R}_{22})=6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U & =2\\cdot {M}_{11}+2\\cdot {M}_{21}+6\\cdot {M}_{12}+6\\cdot {M}_{22} \\\\  & =2{M}_{11}+2{M}_{21}+6{M}_{12}+6{M}_{22}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543560 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186543301 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543560 #edb/ref 1069 "q-123231" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543560 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543560 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[1,4]\\times [2,4]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=16-xy.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{1,2,3,4\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{2,4\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the upper Riemann sum $U(f,P).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543560 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d30a7455-cf28-573b-a7f5-088c618e903c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543560 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](images/de/deff4f8b668e3c7327d92132f579c16d1f99dd5b52603b2f6afe6b7c6c5b7bb6.png)\n\nThe upper sum $U(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={M}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{M}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{M}_{31}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{31}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *maximum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *upper* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=2$ for all $3$ subregions, the formula for $U(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & =2\\cdot {M}_{11}+2\\cdot {M}_{21}+2\\cdot {M}_{31} \\\\  & =2({M}_{11}+{M}_{21}+{M}_{31}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=16-xy$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=16-xy$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/21/21cd2d1c002e5b66100396f9e4d5708b8ffd7fd2b9b6cc7b7078cd5507011a0d.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/9e/9ebca45ee50cf0fe5f91e21427524600b26a512f10340c18c995c16f9cfe372d.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{11} & =f(1,2)=14 \\\\ {M}_{21} & =f(2,2)=12 \\\\ {M}_{31} & =f(3,2)=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & =2(14+12+10) \\\\  & =72.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543569 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186543452 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543569 #edb/ref 1069 "q-123237" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543569 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543569 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[2,4]\\times [1,5]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=21-xy.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{2,3,4\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{1,3,5\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the upper Riemann sum $U(f,P).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543569 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "dfc2de0e-3b59-5c5d-bed1-0d2b8726dbb0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543569 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](images/38/38fcf924a077c207ff66fca76d63333d0f28986432b795c889f22b725faca078.png)\n\nThe upper sum $U(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={M}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{M}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{M}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{M}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22})\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *maximum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *upper* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=2$ for all $4$ subregions, the formula for $U(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & =2\\cdot {M}_{11}+2\\cdot {M}_{21}+2\\cdot {M}_{12}+2\\cdot {M}_{22} \\\\  & =2({M}_{11}+{M}_{21}+{M}_{12}+{M}_{22}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=21-xy$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=21-xy$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/9e/9e1d5a5dcf056f15fdf9e15b4caf3a2f506549ec785c752579bce5b6e12662cb.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/60/609917e6e3e397c9a1bfb4ba92a85535034c657d2bc96ae3b833bea381aea36f.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{11} & =f(2,1)=19 \\\\ {M}_{21} & =f(3,1)=18 \\\\ {M}_{12} & =f(2,3)=15 \\\\ {M}_{22} & =f(3,3)=12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & =2(19+18+15+12) \\\\  & =128.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543574 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186543300 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543574 #edb/ref 1069 "q-123057" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543574 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543574 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/16/16e592cd81e6539e26f10b6bd9352b047576df24b74b4df693f5f2f69799b228.png)\n\nConsider the partition of the rectangular region $R$ shown above and the positive function $f(x,y)$ defined on $R.$ Which of the following gives an expression for the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to this partition.\n\n*Hint: ${M}_{ij}$ denotes the maximum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}$*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543574 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e3f890f2-0602-53b4-b697-bf1bfc15cf9a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543574 #edb/ref 1074 "To calculate the upper Riemann sum $U$ with respect to the given partition, we compute the sum of the volumes of $4$ rectangular solids, one for each ${R}_{ij}.$\n\nThe volume of the rectangular solid corresponding to each subregion ${R}_{ij}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{ij}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{ij}).\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ denotes the maximum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *maximum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *upper* sum.\n\nSo in our case, we have\n\n$$\nU={M}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{M}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{M}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{M}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22}).\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{11})=\\text{Area}({R}_{21})=\\text{Area}({R}_{12})=\\text{Area}({R}_{22})=6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U & =6\\cdot {M}_{11}+6\\cdot {M}_{21}+6\\cdot {M}_{12}+6\\cdot {M}_{22} \\\\  & =6({M}_{11}+{M}_{21}+{M}_{12}+{M}_{22}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543585 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186543440 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543585 #edb/ref 1069 "q-123124" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543585 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543585 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/df/dfba17c3f5744cf122c8051226bc627799bd261b4a5ed6f4d8a03b405dea0c50.png)\n\nConsider the partition of the rectangular region $R$ shown above and the positive function $f(x,y)$ defined on $R.$ Which of the following gives an expression for the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to this partition.\n\n*Hint: ${M}_{ij}$ denotes the maximum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}$*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543585 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "efacd675-1f5e-570d-8835-58b0708fe7ea" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543585 #edb/ref 1074 "To calculate the upper Riemann sum $U$ with respect to the given partition, we compute the sum of the volumes of $4$ rectangular solids, one for each ${R}_{ij}.$\n\nThe volume of the rectangular solid corresponding to each subregion ${R}_{ij}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{ij}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{ij}).\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ denotes the maximum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *maximum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *upper* sum.\n\nSo in our case, we have\n\n$$\nU={M}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{M}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{M}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{M}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22}).\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{11})=\\text{Area}({R}_{21})=\\text{Area}({R}_{12})=\\text{Area}({R}_{22})=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U & =3\\cdot {M}_{11}+3\\cdot {M}_{21}+3\\cdot {M}_{12}+3\\cdot {M}_{22} \\\\  & =3({M}_{11}+{M}_{21}+{M}_{12}+{M}_{22}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
